<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?> 

<section xml:id="section_9-4" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>Chi-square goodness-of-fit test</title>

<subsection> 
 <title>Are birthdays equally distributed throughout the week?</title>
<p>Are the days of the week that women give birth distributed equally throughout 
  the week? Is someone just as likely to be born on a Tuesday as a Saturday? In 
  this Exploration, you will investigate whether there is convincing evidence 
  that birthdays are not distributed equally throughout the week. You will be 
  using a chi-square goodness-of-fit test to help make your conclusion.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection> 
 <title>Step 1: Ask a research question</title>
<activity>
 <!-- Question 1 -->
<statement>
<p>State your research question.</p>
</statement>
<solution>
  <p>
    Are birthdays distributed equally across the days of the week?
  </p>
</solution>
</activity>

</subsection>

<subsection> 
 <title>Step 2: Design a study and collect data</title>
<activity>
 <!-- Question 2 -->
<statement>
<p>What's the categorical variable of interest, and what are the possible categories?</p>
</statement>
<solution>
  <p>
    Days of the week; Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.
  </p>
</solution>
</activity>

<activity>
 <!-- Question 3 -->
<statement>
<p>State the null and alternative hypotheses.</p>
</statement>
<solution>
  <p>
    Null: Birthdays are equally distributed over all seven days of the week (The proportion of birthdays is the same for each day of the week; <m>\pi_{\text{Mon}} = pi_{\text{Tues}} = pi_{\text{Wed}} = pi_{\text{Thurs}} = pi_{\text{Fri}} = pi_{\text{Sat}} = pi_{\text{Sun}} = \frac{1}{7}</m>).
  </p>
  <p>
    Alternative: Birthdays are not equally distributed over all seven days of the week (The proportion of birthdays is not the same for each day of the week; at least one <m>\pi_i</m> is different from 1/7)
  </p>
</solution>
</activity>

<activity>
 <!-- Question 4 -->
<statement>
<p>Write down your own birthday (month/day/year) and those of up to nine of your family members or friends. (Try not to write down a birthday that someone else in the class would write down.)</p>
</statement>
<solution>
  <p>
    Answers will vary.
  </p>
</solution>
</activity>

<activity>
  <statement>
    <p>
      Do an Internet search for “day of birth calculator.” Use the calculator to find 
      out on what day of the week each of your family members/friends was born. Summarize 
      your results in a table.
    </p>
    <table>
      <tabular>
        <row header="yes">
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor">Sun</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Mon</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Tue</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Wed</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Thurs</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Fri</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Sat</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Total</cell>
        </row>
        <row header="yes">
          <cell right="minor">Observed count</cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>
    </table>
  </statement>
  <solution>
    <p>
      Answers will vary.
    </p>
  </solution>
</activity>

<activity>
  <statement>
    <p>
      Combine your results with those for the rest of the class and enter those 
      results in the table.
    </p>
    <table>
      <tabular>
        <row header="yes">
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor">Sun</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Mon</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Tue</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Wed</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Thurs</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Fri</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Sat</cell>
          <cell right="minor">Total</cell>
        </row>
        <row header="yes">
          <cell right="minor">Observed count</cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
          <cell right="minor"></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>
    </table>
  </statement>
  <solution>
    <p>
      Answers will vary.  The fall 2023 class at Grace College had the following data:
    </p>
    <table>
      <tabular>
        <row>
          <cell>
            Sunday
          </cell>
          <cell>
            Monday
          </cell>
          <cell>
            Tuesday
          </cell>
